WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:10.170
We're at a crossing. Can you
feel this? Can you touch the

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:14.490
fear and dizziness of our
moment? Can you sense the ground

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:19.290
shifting beneath you? The sky
spinning as a red tail swipes

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:26.054
the stars from the heavens.
Everything is changing. Right now.

00:00:26.054 --> 00:00:31.560
There's no going back
anymore. All is getting shaky,

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:37.980
but all is getting clamped down.
All is being liberated. While

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:44.280
all is being tracked. All is
permitted, while the inquisitor

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:51.810
looms behind you. Two sides have
risen, insuperable opposites with

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:58.050
no medium to join them. The
extremes are weighing in and all

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:05.280
reality is caught between
Charybdis and Scylla. You see,

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:10.440
they told us the world was just
a cacophony of colliding

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:15.150
particles. That love was just an
injection of hormones and

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:20.970
instincts. They told us the
heavens were cold and dead, that

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:26.190
the fairies were our ancestors'
delusions. They convinced us art

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:31.530
was the framing of random facts
and objects. They told us our

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:35.550
stories and rituals were only
power games and superstitions.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:42.270
They made us into desire
machines, no closer to the gods

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:48.840
than the beasts. In fact, the
gods do not exist. The angels,

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:54.330
the jinns, the demons, the
woodland sprites do not exist.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:01.290
They're superstition. The world
is a wound up clock running out.

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:09.690
And in the end, you are a wound
up clock running out into

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:18.840
nothingness. You can't try to
kill all the gods and then still

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:25.770
expect to live, can you? They
mocked, they derided, they

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:33.360
dissected. And now our world is
being ripped apart. Now who

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:38.370
could have seen this coming? Who
could have thought that in

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:42.570
defiling our stories and
demonizing our orders and

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:47.160
reducing all that made us one,
to the quantities that embodied

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:51.030
that unity. Who would have
thought that that would fragment

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:55.680
us? That it would fragment our
societies, our vision, that it

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:01.800
would twist our virtues into
innumerable empty desires. But

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:08.310
this is where we stand, isn't
it? We look around us and we

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:14.640
watch the story unravel. We
watch our commonalities fall

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:20.970
apart, as people are at each
other's throats. First,

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:29.640
virtually, but more and more in
the flesh. And so what can we

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:39.600
do? We're supposed to be
artists. But it's partly our

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:45.210
fault that this has happened.
Maybe not you and I. But let's

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:51.600
say the artists. We are supposed
to be the guardians of stories.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:59.400
We are supposed to be those who
enchant the world. But for

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:06.450
several hundred years now, it is
us who have played the part in

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:15.210
making everything arbitrary and
making everything random, in

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:22.470
playing around beauty as if it
was just a frivolous fantasy of

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:27.030
individuals. And so it's partly
our fault.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:41.250
And it's partly our fault as
Christians as well. In many ways

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:46.260
we have assaulted the world of
meaning. We have assaulted the

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:56.880
enchanted world. As Christians
we in the West have been part of

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:02.970
those who have removed the
angels from the heavens, who

00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:08.100
have chased the sprites out of
the forests. It's us who did

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:13.170
that. And now we live with the
consequences of our actions.

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:27.760
But hope is not completely lost.
We do stand here in a very dark

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:35.980
moment. We do stand in the dark
room with strange eerie sounds,

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:47.260
coming from that darkness. But
all hope is not lost. We know of

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:53.320
this story. We know of this
story of a man who went into

00:05:53.320 --> 00:06:00.130
death and surprised everybody by
entering there. We know this

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:06.070
story of someone who went into
death and death thought that it

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:11.380
had won. Death thought that in
bringing that man who is also

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:23.170
God into its belly, that it had
won. But it grabbed life. And

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:30.010
the trick was played on it. And
I believe that we can

00:06:30.010 --> 00:06:38.620
participate in that trick. Right
now, all of us, all of us who

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:43.750
are artists and who believe in
that story, who live by that

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:48.880
story, or at least have the
pretence of living by that

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:57.730
story. There's an opportunity
for us right now. Because in

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:04.750
this strange darkness there are
strange creepy crawly things

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:12.850
that are coming up. The world is
being re-enchanted. The

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:20.950
atheists, the secularists, they
were wrong. The world cannot

00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:28.150
exist without meaning. It is
impossible. Every single

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:32.410
capacity we have to even
recognise something as having

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:38.980
being is already a participation
in meaning. Their war on meaning

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:41.050
cannot be won.

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:48.740
But as all of our stories have
been shattered and broken apart,

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:56.900
it has given room for all the
dark things to come back up

00:07:56.900 --> 00:08:00.920
first. And those are the things
we're starting to see appear on

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:07.460
our horizon. The old gods are
coming back and not even the

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:12.500
interesting old gods. But those
darker gods, the ones that don't

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:17.930
have clear identities, those
strange hybrid monsters that

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.450
lived on the edge of the world,
they're the ones that are

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:29.150
crawling back into the world
first. And as artists we have an

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:35.360
opportunity. Because we know the
story, especially as Christian

00:08:35.390 --> 00:08:40.490
artists, we know the story. We
know the story of the world. We

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:47.300
know what happens next. There's
always a spark hidden in the

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:52.940
darkness. There's always a lit
candle in that darkest place.

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:57.830
Because without that lit candle,
things simply do not exist. The

00:08:57.830 --> 00:09:09.470
Word of God is hidden in
creation. And it is our job to

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:16.550
find it, and it is our job as
artists to help the world see

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:26.060
that flicker. And there is an
opportunity, because a strange

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:30.710
thing is happening in culture.
As Christianity is being

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:36.050
evacuated from the public
sphere. As our story is being

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:42.920
tossed aside, it is nonetheless
filling the world at the same

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:48.320
time. And this is a mystery
that, even a few decades ago

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:53.510
people could not see the strange
mystery of death. The strange

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:57.740
mystery of Christ entering in
the tomb we have the opportunity

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:03.080
of seeing it happen right now,
because as the Christian story

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:08.540
is being evacuated, we are
noticing that it's reappearing

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.670
in all the strangest places.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:18.550
Because the bright light of
Christ is no longer so visible,

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:22.510
all of a sudden these small
sparkles are starting to appear

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:28.510
hidden in the cavern walls. And
we see this story of Christ in

00:10:28.510 --> 00:10:34.240
the strangest places we see some
stupid superhero movie where the

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:39.280
superhero falls to the ground
and dies and then rises again.

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:44.650
And we see another strange
popular story coming up of

00:10:44.650 --> 00:10:50.500
someone sacrificing themselves
for others, giving themselves

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:56.770
for the weakest. We see twisted
versions of people who are

00:10:56.770 --> 00:11:01.780
willing to do everything to
bring up the weaker part of our

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:09.070
world, to bolster it and to help
it. And where do you think those

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:21.130
lights come from? And so we have
an opportunity. But we also have

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:26.800
a responsibility. Meaning is
inescapable and we have

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:31.960
responsibility towards it. It is
a weight that we have to carry

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:37.480
as artists. It is a very
daunting responsibility that we

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:42.550
have right now as the world
descends into darkness, that we

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:47.230
are the ones who can give it a
little bit of hope. We are the

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:51.550
ones that can point those little
sparks, those small lights,

00:11:51.550 --> 00:11:55.900
those twisted versions of the
true light, that we are the ones

00:11:55.900 --> 00:12:01.510
who can point it back to the one
true light and origin of our

00:12:01.510 --> 00:12:02.170
world.

00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:15.810
And so I just wanted to maybe
give people a challenge. And I

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:19.920
know all of you watching this
are probably artists. So I want

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:26.790
to give you that challenge. To
jump into that story. To not

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:30.300
think that the story of Christ
is just the story we believe in

00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:35.370
to be saved. But to truly jump
into that story, and realise

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:41.370
that that story is also the
story of everything. It is the

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:45.750
story of creation. It is the
story of how things exist. The

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:51.600
story of Christ is the fullest
manifestation of every other

00:12:51.630 --> 00:12:57.120
story that have been told since
the beginning of time. And so it

00:12:57.120 --> 00:13:01.230
is our responsibility to jump
into that and to redistribute it

00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:06.990
to the world in ways that point
towards that great story. So I

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:12.750
want to thank you for your
attention today. And I hope that

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:17.850
all of us can grasp that
challenge, that opportunity and

00:13:17.850 --> 00:13:19.140
also that responsibility

